y powerful  you know wasn't wasn't wasn't that  effective which was kind of too bad but  in this case they found one not only had  they found this new antibiotic but it's  really good at what it does so that's  great and then the article sums up some  other AI breakthroughs in medicine at  the end for example a drug molecule  discovered by  is going to be used in clinical trials  to treat patients with OCD  another study apparently recently  claimed that AI is more accurate than  doctors in diagnosing breast cancer from  mammograms and so that's great for sort  of the future of medicine to have this  cool new tool I'm not quite sure how I  feel about it all the time I've got a  Google home that frequently tells me  sorry I can't help with that when I add  asked it to add something to the grocery  list or tell me some basic piece of  information and so you know artificial  intelligence is not going to be the may  be the answer to everything right now  but certainly it's come a long way and  is continuing to really push the the  forefront of medicine and that's really  cool so what do you guys think about the  growing problems with antibiotic  resistance is it something that you're  worried about something that you've been  impacted by and then what do you think  about the use of artificial intelligence  there are these new breakthroughs  they're made possible by it do you think  that it's going to be able to replace  humans in the short term or just a great  toolkit to have in our arsenal so let me  know what you think and I look forward  to reading about it in the comments bye
 

